  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Proposal: emit an event after the upload transaction and after a guest download commit",
        "a notifier turns those into emails through a provider, and a preview worker renders thumbnails into the file store",
        "Neither is ever on the request path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "SQLite and the file store (each event fires after a commit there",
        "the preview worker writes its thumbnail into the file store), the router and browsers, and per-workspace access, which has its own question",
        "Connected but out of scope: HTTP server + router, SQLite, File bytes on disk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Constraints",
      "items": [
        "Proposed: side effects (email, previews) fire after the database commit and never inside the request's critical path: an upload or guest download must not fail or slow down because an email provider is slow; this is the rule new features should follow",
        "Run exactly one server process: the in-flight upload set and the login rate limiter live in memory; two instances would each believe they own an upload"
      ]
    }
  ]
